    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p44-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "When 2 dice are rolled, find the probability that the difference of the numbers on the dice is 2.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac29$",
          "worked": "The favourable ordered pairs are $(1,3),(2,4),(3,1),(3,5),(4,2),(4,6),(5,3),(6,4)$.\nThere are 36 equally likely ordered outcomes.\n$$P(\\text{difference }2)=\\frac8{36}=\\frac29.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p44-q9-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Two dice are rolled 50 times. For the binomial distribution of rolling a difference of 2, find:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p44-q9-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the mean",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{100}{9}=11\\dfrac19$",
              "worked": "Let $X$ count rolls with a difference of 2. Then $X\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(50,\\frac29)$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}E(X)&=np\\\\E(X)&=50\\left(\\frac29\\right)\\\\E(X)&=\\frac{100}{9}=11\\frac19.\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 13
          },
          {
            "id": "p44-q9-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "the variance",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{700}{81}=8\\dfrac{52}{81}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=np(1-p)\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=50\\left(\\frac29\\right)\\left(\\frac79\\right)\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\frac{700}{81}=8\\frac{52}{81}.\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 13
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
